  "visual_findings": [
    "The other physical hand (servos 1/2, hand A) was tested with servo 2 fixed at 1212 us. Support servo 4 was prepared at 1474 us; servo 1 went 1537 to 1577, back to 1537, then 1497, back to 1537. The support then returned to 1514 us. All six edges had front and top reviews.",
    "The positive servo-1 edge produced a visible hand/rod/body response and brought the hand visually nearer the body. The negative edge extended the arm outward; the top view also showed a clear change in the associated hand rod. Returns produced visible recovery. This is a powered system response, not proof of a measured servo shaft angle or independent wrist inverse map.",
    "The positive direction also affected the body pose. No completed crossing was observed. Exact joint-coordinate repeatability was not measured; the actual signal at D14 was not tested with an oscilloscope during this trial.",
    "No obvious rod interference, detached rod or curtain exit was visible in the paired reviews. Only the person channels were enabled; servos 3,5,6 and the hand-A pitch stayed fixed during the yaw edges.",
    "The command route closed normally and all ten PWM outputs were switched off at sequence 3512. The original motion locks remained in place."
  ],
